e the Warlords and the Young uncle  and all of this contributes to the  feeling that the world of one piece is  nuanced and multi-dimensional and in  that sense it's a lot like our own world  even though the world of one piece is  full of Fantastical creatures and  locations the culture and politics of  that world are well thought out and  realistic and yet having said all of  that there is one group of people that  seems to break this mold aside from very  few notable exceptions I am of course  talking about the celestial dragons who  are easily the least complex characters  in the entire story I mean they suffer  from a massive God complex and they  consider everyone who is not a world  Noble to be inherently inferior to them  because of this they treat other people  like objects they literally enslave and  abuse whomever they want and laws simply  do not apply to them they can seemingly  do whatever they want whenever they want  and the only person who is allowed to  defy the will of a Celestial Dragon is  another Celestial Dragon herding even a  single Celestial Dragon is so dangerous  that it could lead to the destruction of  an entire Kingdom and so the world  Nobles can get away with pretty much  anything they are easily the least  likable characters in the entire story  as exemplified by Saint Charles the  owner of the most punchable face in the  history of anime the celestial dragons  are so obsessed with the idea that they  are superior to everyone else that they  are often seen wearing outfits that look  like spacesuits and which have an oxygen  tank attached to a glass case that  covers their face they apparently wear  these ridiculous suits because they  don't want to breathe the same air as  lowly commoners the celestial dragons  live on top of the red line in a place  known as the domain of the Gods which is  a sort of holy land that they of course  consider to be superior to all other  locations in the world although some  Celestial dragons such as certain  members of the Don Quixote family have  defied conventions by treating those who  are not World Nobles as actual human  beings worthy of respect this seems to  be a rare exception in the world of the  celestial dragons and all of this really  begs the question why are these  characters so one-dimensional and so  utterly unlikable more importantly why  would the shadow ruler of the world  government prop up these detestable  clowns in ridiculous spacesuits as the  public faces of the world government's  ruling Elite I think we can safely  assume that imusama and the gorosei are  intelligent individuals and capable  rulers so why do they tolerate the  behavior of the celestial dragons surely  they know that the arrogance and cruelty  of the celestial dragons is only  breeding animosity towards the world  government and they have to know that  the ruthless behavior of the world  Nobles creates instability by increasing  the likelihood of rebellion and  resistance from people who are being so  blatantly oppressed and don't even give  me started on those silly space suits at  first many people theorized that the  spacesuits were clues about the true  origins of the celestial dragons  essentially the theory was that they  were from outer space and more  specifically from the Moon we already  know that an advanced civilization once  lived on the moon and their descendants  are the winged people from the various  Sky Islands but the celestial dragons  don't have wings and there's another big  problem here from everything we know  about the world of One Piece you don't  need a spacesuit in order to breathe in  space you can go into space and to the  Moon while just breathing normal air  this may sound crazy at first but we  have to remember that before modern  science actually confirmed that there  was no oxygen in outer space most people  believed that you could in fact breathe  in space many fictional stories that  featured the moon as a setting including  myths fantasies and early science  fiction stories portrayed the moon as  having perfectly breathable oxygen the  world of one p seems to take this false  belief about our own Moon and turns it  into a reality with the moon in one  piece and Al is able to go up to the  moon and hang out there without any sort  of spacesuit a bunch of different space  pirates who seem to be of various races  and species don't use a spacesuit either  and when we see those ancient drawings  on the moon the ones that depict members  of the advanced civilization that used  to reside there those people are not  depicted with any sort of space suit  either so based on the information that  we have so far we have to assume that in  the world of One Piece you don't  actually need a spacesuit to go into  space and that just makes the fact that  Celestial dragons wear what look like  spacesuits even more strange in our  world the suits might indicate that they  came from space or that they are trying  to reference space in some way but in  their world that wouldn't make sense the  only practical purpose of the suits  seems to be avoiding breathing the same  air as commoners and there doesn't  appear to be any deeper meaning behind  it so the only role of these suits is to  make the celestial dragons look as  ridiculous as possible while also  emphasizing the fact that they are cruel  elitists with a superiority complex and  that they treat everyone else like  lesser life forms once again setting up  these people as the public face of the  ruling Elite within the world government  is just the worst possible PR move and  it honestly baffles me that individuals  who are otherwise clearly intelligent  than machiavellians such as imusama  decided to set up a system that is just  inviting people to rebel against it I  mean how much smarter would it be to  just make the celestial dragons appear  benevolent and generous in public  imagine if they brought gifts for the  poor in every Kingdom they visited  imagine if they at least pretended to be  kind and compassionate towards the  people that they ruled over imagine if  they demonstrated even basic competence  when it comes to statesmanship if they  behaved in this way even if it was all  just an act it would make it much easier  to keep the people obedient even if the  actual political system within the world  government didn't change at all just  making these simple surface level public  relations changes to the way that the  celestial dragons are perceived would go  a long way to perpetuating the world  government system and discouraging  people from joining revolutionary  movements or sympathizing with pirates  and yet imusama and the gorosei have  chosen to preside over a system that is  almost designed to make everyone hate  the celestial dragons and speaking of  the gorosei notice how despite also  being Celestial dragons they don't wear  ridiculous spacesuits they don't have  cringy hair buns and they don't act  pompous and obnoxious towards those who  are not World Nobles for example they  are perfectly willing to meet with  Shanks in private and when they do meet  with them they don't seem worried about  breathing the same air as him or having  him bow before them the goros say  clearly know what Smart statesmanship  looks like they know how to leaders and  they make those spacesuit wearing World  Nobles look absolutely goofy by  comparison and I think that this is the  key point the vast majority of the  celestial dragons are goofy  one-dimensional villains with extremely  punchable faces because that is exactly  what they were always supposed to be  they are mere puppets of imusama and the  gorosei and they are simply playing the  role that the true ruler of the world  government had assigned to them without  them even realizing it in other words  aside from the gorosei the celestial  dragons are nothing but pawns who are  about to be sacrificed by imusama in  order to preserve his or her power I  believe that imusama is well aware that  big changes to the structure of the  world are on the horizon the return of  Joy boy has long been foretold the  Golden Age of the Pirates has been  shaking things up for over two decades  the Revolutionary Army is on the rise  and so on the many enemies of the world  government are amassing and they are  getting stronger Luffy has awakened the  Nika fruit and is stronger than ever  Blackbeard is also getting more and more  dangerous the revolutionaries are making  serious inroads and all of them see the  celestial dragons as their enemy all of  them want to put an end to the corrupt  system that places the world Nobles at  the top and everyone else below them  except we know that the world Nobles are  not really at the top everyone just  thinks that they are the empty Throne is  not really empty although it's occupant  imusama has gone out of his or her way  to keep his or her existence a secret so  what is imusama really up to many fans  have speculated that imusama has  actually been alive for a very long time  perhaps even since the void Century if  this is true then imusama knows how the  world Works imusama knows that military  con conflicts and drastic political  changes are inevitable and that they  happen in Cycles over the course of  decades and centuries when you push  people far enough they will inevitably  fight back and this will lead to the  collapse of one political regime and the  rise of another so what if imusama has  been preparing for this very thing what  if the celestial dragons are supposed to  be one-dimensional and obnoxious  villains because they were always  intended to be sacrificed and replaced  with a different ruling Elite while the  actual ruler behind the scenes Remains  the Same a lot of us have wondered why  imusama had four photos in his or her  possession photos which show the Luffy  Blackbeard shirahoshi and Vivi the other  three photos were all damaged in some  way either ripped or stabbed but vi